Apple today released <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a> Classical version 4.1, with a new black-and-white app icon and an updated interface.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/apple-music-classical-hero.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076044" /><br/>
The redesigned icon retains the app's treble clef, but now rendered in shaded black against a white background. The change brings &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; Classical in line with &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj;'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/21/apple-music-new-look-announced/">new visual identity</a>, which Apple introduced last month, replacing its familiar red branding with a monochrome appearance.<br/>
<br/>
The new version of the app also features blue accents for selected tabs, playback buttons, and links, instead of the previous red ones. Apple has not detailed the visual changes in its release notes, which state only that the update contains "stability and performance enhancements."<br/>
<br/>
